  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945897/assets/b8fdc38797fd763fbffccccd7ca7e6cdc39ce99445440e9ebb918ef11d5c23d9.png)\n\nFind the area of the triangle $\u25b3ABC.$\n\n(Figure not drawn to scale)",
  "worked_solution": "The area of the triangle is defined as\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nWe can see that the base is $BC=4$ and the corresponding height is $AH=6.$ Therefore, the area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 6}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{2} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
